    "result": "I implemented `RateLimiter` in `solution.py` and wrote a 54-test pytest suite in `tests/test_solution.py`; `python -m pytest -q tests` passes with all 54 tests. Each client keeps a list of `(time, cost)` records, and a record counts while `now - t < window_seconds`, so a request exactly one window old is released. `allow` records only when it accepts, while `remaining` and `retry_after` record nothing. `retry_after` walks the client's records oldest-first until enough units would be freed, and returns the time until the last of those expires. Constructor, cost and time checks raise `ValueError` as the spec requires, and a rejected cost does not advance the limiter's clock. I did not run the coverage, CRAP, mutation or bandit gates; the code is small and each branch has a test, but those gates are unverified.",
